# Local dev services (keep usable / session hygiene)

**测完可复测第一 — 但人停了就别再起。** Delivery or land does **not** mean tear down a localhost stack the human still needs. It also does **not** mean resurrect anything the human (or an aborted-shell notification) just stopped.

## Keep available (required — only when still up)

After implement / UAT / merge in this thread, **if a healthy product web for this checkout is already listening**:

1. Leave it up (`npm run dev` / the port used for UAT). Leave **local Supabase** running when this thread used `npm run dev` + supabase-local.
2. Report the live base in the closing note (`http://localhost:<port>`, `MESA_UAT_BASE` if not `:3000`).
3. Prefer **reuse** an already-healthy server that serves this checkout over starting a disposable second instance then killing everything.

Do **not** start a new web solely because UAT/land finished and nothing is listening.

## Human stop / aborted shell (hard)

If Will stops a listen port, kills a terminal, or a system notification says a **this-thread** `next dev` / `npm run dev|cloud|stage` / ops shell was **aborted** / **terminated_by_user**:

1. **Do not restart it.** Brief note only (“已停”).
2. Aborted-task “follow-up” does **not** authorize relaunching web/dev/ops/print-agent.
3. Restart only when Will **explicitly** asks in-thread（例如「再起 web」「起 :3005」）.

## Session hygiene (allowed)

To cut noise / CPU, you may stop processes that are **clearly started by this thread** and **not** needed for further testing of this checkout — e.g. a second Next on `:3002+` when a healthy primary for the same checkout remains, or a finished one-shot build/lint shell.

Before stopping anything: confirm PID/cwd/port belong to **this** conversation’s commands (terminal metadata / the PID you spawned).

## Forbidden

- Killing or reclaiming a listen port / agent / `npm run dev|cloud|stage` / ops / print-agent you did **not** start in this thread (includes other Cursor chats and human terminals) — same spirit as [`dev-port-isolation.mdc`](./dev-port-isolation.mdc)
- **Auto-restarting** a web/dev/ops process after Will stopped it or after an aborted-shell notification
- `supabase db reset`, `docker compose down -v`, deleting local DB volumes, or any hard local DB wipe — unless the user explicitly asks in-thread
- Stopping local Supabase / Docker DB “for cleanup” after UAT
- Ending the **only** remaining healthy web for this checkout just because the task checklist is done — **unless Will already stopped it / asked to stop**
- Broad `pkill -f next` / `killall node` / port-wide kills that can hit other sessions

## Order of operations (end of thread)

1. If a usable web (+ local Supabase if used) is **still up**, leave it; report the base.
2. Optionally stop **this-thread-only** redundant extras.
3. Do **not** touch other sessions’ agents or the local database.
4. Do **not** start a replacement web because ports are empty after a human stop.
